{
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "ADP-PCCC-PILOT",
      "title": "pilot: omni-plc-sim PCCC (micrologix1400 profile) -> pccc adapter -> file",
      "intent": "The first case on a real PCCC server: SFC's own EtherNet/IP client (RegisterSession, then SendRRData with CIP Execute PCCC and CMD 0x0F FNC 0xA2 typed reads) against omni-plc-sim's MicroLogix 1400 data table, with channels in every file type the adapter decodes (O, I, S, B, T, C, R, N, F, ST, L, A), through the read optimiser, in all three deployment modes. If it fails, SFC no longer reads SLC 500 or MicroLogix controllers: a regression in framing, address encoding, the optimiser or a decoder. Static values are exact; the dynamic block (the F8:10..21 signals, N7:10/11, L10:10, the S:4 clock, the self-resetting timer T4:1 and the counter C5:1) is range- and change-checked over 8 records (the first read waits out the TCP client's 1 s first-send delay, so the second follows it back to back). The simulator's events log proves the wire plan (15 requests a cycle, F8 and L10 split by the 32-byte MaxReadGap) and that no request got an error status. Client defects avoided: O/I addresses with .n and O/I arrays on their own (the size sent and the length expected disagree, Address.kt:26-51 vs :301-308), B3:0.1 (the .1 is ignored) and C5:0.0 (word 0 as an INT, not a bit), reconnects and config reloads (no new RegisterSession, and cached packets keep the first session handle: Client.kt:146, PcccSource.kt:48-56), ConnectPath (never applied: PcccControllerConfiguration.kt:20-22) and non-ASCII text (bytes decoded as signed chars, Decoders.kt:33-53).",
      "pins": [
        "adapters/pccc/src/main/kotlin/com/amazonaws/sfc/pccc/protocol/Client.kt:66-136",
        "adapters/pccc/src/main/kotlin/com/amazonaws/sfc/pccc/protocol/Client.kt:224-243",
